{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-26T15:07:32.203Z","data":{"text":"I implemented the OpenCode v2 adapter changes and wrote the result file, but hit a genuine planning conflict that I must flag rather than work around.\n\n## What I did\n\n**`src/harness/opencode/opencode.ts`**\n- `buildOpencodeArgs`: `run <prompt> --standalone --agent <agent> --auto --format json --model <model>`; no `--dir`, no `--variant`; `variant` folded as `<model>#<variant>`.\n- `spawn`: tracks streamed usage in a parser closure, then after exit runs `opencode session export --standalone <sessionID>` (bounded by `timeouts.harnessPreflightSeconds`, 10 default) and appends the clamped field-wise remainder `tokens` event only when non-zero.\n- `spawnInteractive`: `opencode mini --prompt <prompt>` plus `--model`/`--agent`.\n- `preflightOpencode`: uses `assessOpencodeVersion`, exits 1 with the diagnostics message below 2.0.0.\n- Extracted `emitOpencodeTokensEvent` to keep `processOpencodeStdoutLine` under the 80-line budget.\n\n**New** `src/harness/opencode/opencode-session.ts`: tracker, export parser, `readOpencodeSessionUsage`, remainder computation, append.\n\n**Tests**: new `tests/opencode-v2.test.ts` + fixtures copied from `observed/`; updated the v1 argument assertions in `tests/opencode-spawn.test.ts` and `tests/harness-interactive.test.ts`. **README** opencode section updated.\n\n`node --import tsx --test tests/opencode-v2.test.ts` passes (4/4), as do typecheck, lint, and function/line budgets.\n\n## The blocker\n\n`tests/watcher-preflight.test.ts` is **not in this task's scope** and is frozen. Its first case fakes `opencode 1.0.0` and expects preflight to succeed, but the required \"preflight refuses opencode 1\" behavior now calls `process.exit(1)`, killing that test process. The one-line fix is to change that fake to `opencode 2.0.0`. I did not touch it, because doing so would trip the watcher's `undeclared_test_change` gate (only `tests/opencode-spawn.test.ts` and `tests/harness-interactive.test.ts` are authorized). So `pnpm verify` stays red until the task scope is widened.\n\nDetails are in `openspec/changes/092-opencode-v2-adapter/.run/results/2.md` under `## Missing context`, `## Outside scope`, and `## Blocked`."}}
